# Tests — MSA Schedule 4 Service Credits

Assertion-based tests for `Service_credits`. The L-4.1 band table is a
staircase whose boundaries are money, so every one of them is tested exactly
on the boundary as well as one hundredth of a percentage point below it:
99.90, 99.50, 99.00, 98.00 and 95.00. Each boundary is inclusive downwards
("not less than 99.50%") and exclusive upwards ("less than 99.90%"), and
getting either the wrong way round changes what the Customer is paid.

99.90 is the case worth stating twice: L-4.1 engages only where the
Availability Percentage is *less than* 99.90%, so at exactly 99.90% there is
no credit at all — not band (a)'s 5%.

L-4.3 is tested as the two-part override it is: below 95.00% both the cap and
the credit become 50%, and neither alone would produce 50% of the Monthly
Service Charge. L-4.4 is tested on both sides of "more than 30 days", with the
`invoice_undisputed` judgement input both ways, and against an L-4.3 credit as
well as an L-4.1 one.

The last two tests run the L-2.3 rounding through to the money, because that
is where the rounding rule is actually felt.

> Using Availability
> Using ServiceCredits

## L2_7_MonthlyServiceCharge

L-2.7: the three excluded categories come off the charges for the Service.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_7_MonthlyServiceCharge:
  output r content ServiceCredits.MonthlyServiceCharge

scope TestL2_7_MonthlyServiceCharge:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.MonthlyServiceCharge with {
      -- charges_for_the_service: $12,000.00
      -- one_off_charges: $1,000.00
      -- professional_services_charges: $500.00
      -- pass_through_charges: $200.00
    }
  assertion r.monthly_service_charge = $10,300.00
```

## L2_7_NothingToExclude

L-2.7: with none of the three excluded categories present the base is the
whole of the charges for the Service.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_7_NothingToExclude:
  output r content ServiceCredits.MonthlyServiceCharge

scope TestL2_7_NothingToExclude:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.MonthlyServiceCharge with {
      -- charges_for_the_service: $10,000.00
      -- one_off_charges: $0.00
      -- professional_services_charges: $0.00
      -- pass_through_charges: $0.00
    }
  assertion r.monthly_service_charge = $10,000.00
```

## L4_1_ServiceLevelMet

L-4.1 base case: the Service Level was met, so no credit is payable.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_ServiceLevelMet:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_ServiceLevelMet:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 99.99
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_cap_percentage = 30%
  assertion r.credit_payable_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $0.00
```

## L4_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNine

L-4.1 engages only "where the Availability Percentage ... is less than
99.90%". At exactly 99.90% the Service Level is met under L-3.1 and there is
no credit — band (a) does not reach up to 99.90%.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNine:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNine:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 99.90
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_payable_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $0.00
```

## L4_1_BandA_JustBelow

L-4.1(a): the first hundredth of a percentage point below the Service Level
carries 5%.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_BandA_JustBelow:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_BandA_JustBelow:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 99.89
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 5%
  assertion r.credit_cap_percentage = 30%
  assertion r.credit_payable_percentage = 5%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $500.00
```

## L4_1_BandA_ExactlyNinetyNinePointFive

L-4.1(a): "but not less than 99.50%" is inclusive, so exactly 99.50% is band
(a) at 5% and not band (b) at 10%.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_BandA_ExactlyNinetyNinePointFive:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_BandA_ExactlyNinetyNinePointFive:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 99.50
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 5%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $500.00
```

## L4_1_BandB_JustBelowNinetyNinePointFive

L-4.1(b): one hundredth lower and the credit doubles to 10%.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_BandB_JustBelowNinetyNinePointFive:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_BandB_JustBelowNinetyNinePointFive:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 99.49
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 10%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $1,000.00
```

## L4_1_BandB_ExactlyNinetyNine

L-4.1(b): "but not less than 99.00%" is inclusive, so exactly 99.00% is band
(b) at 10% and not band (c) at 20%.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_BandB_ExactlyNinetyNine:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_BandB_ExactlyNinetyNine:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 99.00
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 10%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $1,000.00
```

## L4_1_BandC_JustBelowNinetyNine

L-4.1(c): 20%.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_BandC_JustBelowNinetyNine:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_BandC_JustBelowNinetyNine:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 98.99
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 20%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $2,000.00
```

## L4_1_BandC_ExactlyNinetyEight

L-4.1(c): "but not less than 98.00%" is inclusive, so exactly 98.00% is band
(c) at 20% and not band (d) at 30%.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_BandC_ExactlyNinetyEight:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_BandC_ExactlyNinetyEight:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 98.00
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 20%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $2,000.00
```

## L4_1_BandD_JustBelowNinetyEight

L-4.1(d): 30%, which is also exactly the L-4.2 cap, so the cap does not bite.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_BandD_JustBelowNinetyEight:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_BandD_JustBelowNinetyEight:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 97.99
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 30%
  assertion r.credit_cap_percentage = 30%
  assertion r.credit_payable_percentage = 30%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $3,000.00
```

## L4_3_ExactlyNinetyFive

L-4.3 applies where the Availability Percentage is "less than 95.00%", which
is strict. At exactly 95.00% L-4.1(d) still governs: 30% credit, 30% cap.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_3_ExactlyNinetyFive:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_3_ExactlyNinetyFive:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 95.00
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 30%
  assertion r.credit_cap_percentage = 30%
  assertion r.credit_payable_percentage = 30%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $3,000.00
```

## L4_3_JustBelowNinetyFive

L-4.3: one hundredth lower and both the credit and the cap become 50%. Both
halves of L-4.3 are needed for this figure — with the cap left at 30% the
payable percentage would be 30%, and with the credit left at band (d)'s 30%
the raised cap would make no difference.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_3_JustBelowNinetyFive:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_3_JustBelowNinetyFive:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 94.99
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 50%
  assertion r.credit_cap_percentage = 50%
  assertion r.credit_payable_percentage = 50%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $5,000.00
```

## L4_3_FarBelowNinetyFive

L-4.3: 50% is the whole of the remedy however bad the month, since L-4.3 also
sets the maximum aggregate.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_3_FarBelowNinetyFive:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_3_FarBelowNinetyFive:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 50.00
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 50%
  assertion r.credit_cap_percentage = 50%
  assertion r.credit_payable_percentage = 50%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $5,000.00
```

## L4_4_ThirtyOneDaysInArrears

L-4.4: "more than 30 days" in arrears of an undisputed invoice forfeits the
credit entirely.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_4_ThirtyOneDaysInArrears:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_4_ThirtyOneDaysInArrears:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 98.00
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 31
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_payable_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $0.00
```

## L4_4_ThirtyDaysInArrears

L-4.4: exactly 30 days is not "more than 30 days", so the band (c) credit
survives.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_4_ThirtyDaysInArrears:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_4_ThirtyDaysInArrears:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 98.00
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 30
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 20%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $2,000.00
```

## L4_4_DisputedInvoice

L-4.4 bites only on an "undisputed" invoice. That characterisation is the
judgement input: with it false, long arrears forfeit nothing.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_4_DisputedInvoice:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_4_DisputedInvoice:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 98.00
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 365
      -- invoice_undisputed: false
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 20%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $2,000.00
```

## L4_4_DefeatsL4_3

L-4.4 forfeits the credit "in respect of a Measurement Period", so it defeats
L-4.3's 50% and not only the L-4.1 bands. The cap is unaffected — L-4.4 says
nothing about the maximum aggregate — but there is nothing left to cap.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_4_DefeatsL4_3:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_4_DefeatsL4_3:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 94.00
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 31
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_cap_percentage = 50%
  assertion r.credit_payable_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $0.00
```

## L4_4_ArrearsInAGoodMonth

L-4.4 repeats L-4.1's condition, so in a month where the Service Level was met
it changes nothing: the answer is already no credit, under L-4.1's base case
rather than under L-4.4.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_4_ArrearsInAGoodMonth:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_4_ArrearsInAGoodMonth:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 99.95
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 90
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $0.00
```

## L4_1_CreditOnTheL2_7Base

The percentage applies to the Monthly Service Charge as L-2.7 defines it, not
to the gross charges: 20% of $10,300.00, not of $12,000.00.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_1_CreditOnTheL2_7Base:
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestL4_1_CreditOnTheL2_7Base:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: 98.50
      -- monthly_service_charge:
          (output of ServiceCredits.MonthlyServiceCharge with {
             -- charges_for_the_service: $12,000.00
             -- one_off_charges: $1,000.00
             -- professional_services_charges: $500.00
             -- pass_through_charges: $200.00
           }).monthly_service_charge
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 20%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $2,060.00
```

## Integration_RoundingDeniesTheCredit

L-2.3 and L-4.1 together. A 30-day Measurement Period with 45 Unavailable
Minutes is an unrounded 99.8958%, and the Availability Percentage — the
rounded figure, which is what L-4.1 compares — is 99.90%. No credit.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestIntegration_RoundingDeniesTheCredit:
  internal availability content decimal
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestIntegration_RoundingDeniesTheCredit:
  definition availability equals
    (output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
       -- total_minutes: 43200
       -- minutes_not_available: 45
       -- excluded_minutes: 0
       -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 0
     }).availability_percentage
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: availability
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion availability = 99.90
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 0%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $0.00
```

## Integration_OneMoreMinuteEarnsFivePercent

One further Unavailable Minute gives an unrounded 99.8935%, an Availability
Percentage of 99.89%, and a credit of 5% — $500.00 turning on a single
minute and on the rounding rule in L-2.3.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestIntegration_OneMoreMinuteEarnsFivePercent:
  internal availability content decimal
  output r content ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit

scope TestIntegration_OneMoreMinuteEarnsFivePercent:
  definition availability equals
    (output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
       -- total_minutes: 43200
       -- minutes_not_available: 46
       -- excluded_minutes: 0
       -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 0
     }).availability_percentage
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCredits.ServiceCredit with {
      -- availability_percentage: availability
      -- monthly_service_charge: $10,000.00
      -- arrears_days: 0
      -- invoice_undisputed: true
    }
  assertion availability = 99.89
  assertion r.credit_percentage = 5%
  assertion r.credit_amount = $500.00
```
